<title>USA: ITT to sell N. American aftermarket unit.</title>
<headline>ITT to sell N. American aftermarket unit.</headline>
<dateline>AUBURN HILLS, Mich. 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>ITT Automotive, a unit of ITT Industries Inc, said Tuesday was selling its North American Aftermarket division to Echlin Inc for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>The ITT Automotive division will operate as Aimco Products Inc, a division of Echlin's North American Aftermarket Operations. The unit's annual sales are about $140 million.</p>
<p>ITT will continue to own and operate its aftermarket unit in Europe, the company said.</p>
</text>
